2026-10-22T16:58:19.0820041Z    image gate: coleman_ames_house_1811_prairie inland_architect_plate: verdict "differs", 6 difference(s) open: the bay's south-return downpipe: the plate's pale rod at x 298-302 px, from a head under the bay's cornice, runs down the return's own south face about 0.3 m in from the front's corner (a 1.0 m return at v 5.99 hides the main wall from x 288 to 315 px, so it cannot stand on the main front there); K01's front pipes run only along the street front, so T-2993 stands it on the main front beside the return at 6.24 m, landing at x 320-326 px, about 21 px south of the plate's (T-2997); the oriel's depth and returns: the plate's oriel is a flat-fronted box about 3 m across (x 338-470 px) about 0.6 m out, its south return lit by two or three narrow lights and stood on a rounded rock-faced base; the build's stands 0.5 m out on canted returns with none, on K08's three corbel courses (0.52 m at most). T-3005's re-read: the return reads 27 px wide (x 470-497), which a square 0.6 m return cannot fill from this camera (about 9 px): it follows the entrance block's ROUNDED south corner under it (T-3006), so the oriel waits on that corner (T-3007); the porch's south return: beside the arch, from about x 467 to 507 px, the plate opens the entrance block's south return as a small arcade of round-arched lights on colonnettes with carved capitals, lighting the porch from the side; the build closes it in coursed stone (T-2991); the arcade's capitals (y 680-690 px) and crowns (y 647-660) step down across x 476-501, so it stands on a face receding from the front, about v 9.4-9.5 by the camera, short of the solved south corner at v 10.40; T-3005's re-read: the corner is ROUNDED, about 0.9 m radius, its front tangent at x 467-470 (v about 9.5) and its far side at about x 515-520 (the solve's x 510 is that edge), the downpipe's shoe at about y 816 px on the south face just behind it; the colonnettes step down because they run round the curve (on a 0.9 m radius, x 476, 490 and 501 px stand at about 8, 27 and 44 degrees from the front), not along a flat return. K01 has no rounded corner (T-3006); the arcade then stands on it (T-2991); the bay's stone gable's centre: its apex, its lights and its pinnacles stand about 10 px (0.25 m) south of the plate's (the apex at x about 209 px against 196, the flat-headed lights' centre at 208 against 197), as T-2542 placed the gable on the bay's centre; and the plate's pinnacles are carved, the right-hand one capped by a scaled dome, the left by a moulded block, where the build's are square shafts under pyramids (T-2920); the roof's shape: the plate's main roof reads as a steep hipped mass whose apex stands over the bay (x 320 px, about v 4 m), its south slope falling behind the oriel to a lower roof (top about 13 m) that runs to the tall stack; the build lays K01's one ridge along the whole front at 16.0 m, so it shows slate where the plate shows sky over the south half (x 400-500 px, y 240-340 px); the stacks: the plate's tall stack with its corbelled cap on the south gable and the range's second stack (x about 545 px); the build's two plain stacks stand behind the ridge where this camera does not see them
