2026-10-22T16:58:19.0973916Z    image gate: wheeler_house_1812_prairie levy_front: verdict "differs", 19 difference(s) open: Gable: each shoulder stone carries a sunk panel; built plain; Gable: the grid window stands in quoined side stones under a moulded hood with a wavy upper edge, over a deep moulded shelf; built with K06's own sill and no surround or hood; Gable: the grid window's lights read as dark openings; K06's casement frame reads heavier at 0.44 by 0.37 m; Gable: the kneelers' scrolls are carved; built as a plain roll with a raised eye; Balcony: the middle of its front run (x 390-680 px) is a solid stone panel rising to a central pedestal, with iron scrolls against it; built as more of the iron rail, its balusters plain square bars without the print's roundels; South projection: its top, K08's 0.2 m fascia over the 9.45 m wall head, renders about 25-30 px over the print's cornice, and the balcony stands on it, about as high again; Third storey: the large window's middle light is wider than the two beside it and carries an arched head of its own, and its fanlight has a concentric bar as well as radial ones; built as three equal lights under a radial fanlight; Third storey: the small arched window is filled with a patterned light or panel; built as a round fanlight sash; Third storey: the voussoirs alternate long and short into the brick; built as a ring of equal stones standing 0.1 m before the wall; Second storey: the north window's transom lights are glazed in small squares; built as one plate light each; Gable: from the kneelers (about 11.6-11.7 m) to the ledge (12.55 m) the slab's base runs out square past the side walls, where the print's outline is already drawing in; Entrance: the arch's south jamb and moulding run down the projection's north corner in the print (its outer moulding at about x 740-755 px), so the arch reads about 0.3 m further south and broader; the build stands its 2.7 m mouth clear of the projection, from 5.2 m; Entrance: the arch is turned in a narrow moulded ring of light stone, and its curve is flatter at the crown than a segment (nearer a half ellipse); built as K01's voussoir block on a segmental head with a keystone flush with the ring; Entrance: the transom under the fanlight is a heavy moulded beam about 0.25 m deep, and the fanlight's three lights are divided by narrow columns of small panes; built as K07's 0.07 m bar and three plain lights; Stair: the north cheek flares out as it sweeps down and both end in a carved newel under a cap; built straight, to a plain block; Carving: the frieze is an interlace of crossing straps and leaves and the bosses carved shields; built as T-2819's guilloche of rings and plain oval bosses in a moulded ring; South projection: the second storey's jamb stones rise past the window's head to small carved caps under the projection's cornice; built stopping at the head; Tone: the print's stone reads lighter than its brick; the built brown sandstone renders darker than the buff brick beside it (the colours are not shown, the relation is); Roof: the steep slated slopes the photograph shows behind the gable's shoulders, flat-topped like a mansard's; built as K01's hip (T-2545)
